1
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:26,860
Floating on the Nakagawa River,
aiming for one particular day,

2
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:34,000
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:42,220
Right onto the head of a
carpenter who had been saving up,

4
00:00:42,220 --> 00:00:48,460
they laughed at me for
still acting like a brat.

5
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:55,260
Even if you lose your spirit,
Katsushika is always there.

6
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:58,620
Another yawn, and nothing changes.

7
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:02,540
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:10,460
From the pointed-hat water intake tower,

9
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:16,800
the setting sun sinks toward
the great Shaku Tenmon.

10
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:25,260
I wonder how tomorrow will end too.

11
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,260
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness is lost again.

12
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:33,860
Because I'm the fool
who finally realized it.

13
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:41,860
Eight-hour trip around the world

14
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:48,880
Reading foreign magazines again, are you?

15
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:50,020
Which country's is that?

16
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:52,720
It's a magazine for young French women.

17
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:54,760
It's full of useful stuff.

18
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:57,280
Just looking at foreign writing makes me

19
00:01:57,280 --> 00:01:59,240
dizzy. How can you stand it?

20
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:00,960
Hey, Nakagawa.

21
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:03,860
Did you say something, senpai?

22
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:06,400
And this one's an English newspaper

23
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:09,280
You two really don't look like
police officers from the old town.

24
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:15,880
Isn't that the crackpot professor?
It really is Professor Ezaki.

25
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:25,620
What about Professor Ezaki? Apparently he's presenting some research at a conference in New York.
It's his research, so it's bound to be junk anyway.

26
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:29,200
What is it?

27
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,960
It's a gissha, you know.

28
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:34,800
Really?

29
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:37,660
I've got a bad feeling about this.

30
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:42,940
Everyone, it's been a long time!

31
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:44,080
See? Told you so.

32
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,560
Professor Ezaki.

33
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,620
How creepy.

34
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:54,960
I, who have lived in every
country in the world until now,

35
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:59,420
have come to the conclusion that Japan is
the most wonderful country in the world, oja.

36
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:03,360
It's certainly very Japanese, though.

37
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:06,400
Frankly,
you've got the wrong idea there, you know.

38
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:10,440
Aren't you the only decent one here,
at least this side of Nishikigoe?

39
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:12,920
Hey, what are you doing, anyway?

40
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,440
You mustn't peek with that dirty face.

41
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:18,400
That koi costs a million yen a fish, oja.

42
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:21,040
A million yen per fish?

43
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:22,260
So that means...

44
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:24,860
For civilian Japanese use,

45
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:27,520
since when, seven nights?

46
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:28,460
and...

47
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:31,080
That's definitely over 20 million.

48
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:34,020
Always getting treated terribly,

49
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:35,800
if you think of it as consolation money,

50
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:36,760
it's not so bad.

51
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:38,180
Master.

52
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:41,760
The outdoor tea ceremony is ready.

53
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:43,600
Hey, thanks.

54
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:45,320
"Thanks"? What's that supposed to mean?

55
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,360
"Thanks" is the money you took.

56
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:50,180
An old hag like her
taking a day off? No way!

57
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:52,940
Yes, I took it. Thank you for allowing me.

58
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:53,560
What?

59
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:59,980
Thank you for always looking out for me,
for the past forty years.

60
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:04,320
Let me introduce you.

61
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:07,160
This is Kiyo, who has served
our Ezaki family for generations

62
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:10,140
and who takes care of me, Kiyo-san, de oja.

63
00:04:10,940 --> 00:04:13,560
Please, everyone, take good care of me.

64
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:16,460
Well then, this way, please.

65
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:20,220
The tea ceremony is the very
origin of Japan's wabi-sabi, de oja.

66
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:22,568
The heart of tea is a mother's heart.

67
00:04:22,618 --> 00:04:25,331
Drink it and the fountain of
life flows through you, de oja.

68
00:04:25,381 --> 00:04:26,960
Here, please, help yourself.

69
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:31,200
Ryuho!

70
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:35,600
Here you go.

71
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:39,580
Well then, I'll gratefully receive it.

72
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:48,060
Very fine tea indeed.

73
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:50,500
I'm just going to the toilet for a moment.

74
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:11,180
Twenty million, twenty million!

75
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:12,480
Wait just a moment!

76
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:12,960
Gulp!

77
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:17,220
What's in that trash can?

78
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:21,560
I'm going to check it. Well, this is

79
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:27,020
What's the matter, Ryo-chan?
You've done something again, haven't you?

80
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:29,280
I didn't do anything!

81
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:36,060
Stop playing dumb.
This is the best evidence there is!

82
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:39,580
Senpai, the koi in the pond!

83
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:42,780
Goodness, you really can't let your
guard down for a second with you around.

84
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:45,540
What's he going on about?

85
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:47,520
Don't look too closely, you know.

86
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:49,760
That's not a foreign language,
that's just a normal voice, right?

87
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:52,640
Now that you mention it,

88
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:54,600
It's pitch black, isn't it.

89
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,120
So that's how it is.

90
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:57,600
This is a problem.

91
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:59,900
I'm going to be wrongly accused.

92
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:00,940
Be quiet!

93
00:06:00,940 --> 00:06:02,980
You might fool the others,

94
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:05,720
but you won't fool this master's eyes!

95
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:08,400
Exactly, that's right.

96
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:09,840
I won't be fooled!

97
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:10,640
Hah.

98
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:19,120
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

99
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:21,780
Fallen off...
the pattern shows through from underneath.

100
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:27,100
As you can see, I painted over it
with black to cover it up, Ryo-chan.

101
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:30,280
Just as expected of you, master.

102
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:34,340
I'm impressed you saw
through this trick at a glance.

103
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:38,980
Hah-hah-hah! No need to be so tense,
no need at all, I tell you.

104
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:43,080
Acting so high and mighty,
when you didn't understand a thing!

105
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:48,240
What are you talking about?
The master saw all of this coming!

106
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:54,280
It's turned black again.

107
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:54,820
What?

108
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,120
The real one is...

109
00:06:58,760 --> 00:06:59,560
over here.

110
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,980
Splendid work, master.

111
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:08,440
To hide the real one beforehand, paint an ordinary carp,
and release it into the pond, how clever.

112
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:11,760
Precisely so, indeed.

113
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:14,040
I knew everything all along, you see.

114
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:17,540
Amazing, and Kiyo-san did all of it!

115
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:19,800
You really do give the professor all the credit,
don't you.

116
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:23,500
This old woman is no ordinary person.

117
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:25,544
Hohoh, by the way, gentlemen,

118
00:07:25,594 --> 00:07:28,340
today I have something else
I'd like to show you, oja.

119
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:33,760
This is the videotape I'll be using when I present at the upcoming conference,
you see.

120
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:36,021
Once this is presented,

121
00:07:36,071 --> 00:07:39,260
the whole world will
take notice of my theory.

122
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:42,820
Allow me to show this tape
to you all ahead of time.

123
00:07:43,340 --> 00:07:45,810
Haa, haha, Ezaki Korosuke,

124
00:07:45,860 --> 00:07:47,660
two, that's all there is to it.

125
00:07:47,660 --> 00:07:48,280
One, two, one.

126
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:51,060
We're perfectly in sync.

127
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:53,980
Damn it, you goddamn old hag!

128
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:54,900
Just you wait.

129
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:00,940
Hmph.

130
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:07,500
Yuuk Hunter

131
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:09,800
Operation Oge-retsu

132
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,280
Mmm~ hah~

133
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:12,180
W-wait, what?

134
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:15,620
Hey, what were you going to do, present
something like this at the academic conference?

135
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:17,460
N-no, no, wrong, wrong!

136
00:08:17,460 --> 00:08:19,315
No, not this one. Not this one either.

137
00:08:19,365 --> 00:08:21,720
That tape, where did that tape go?!

138
00:08:22,180 --> 00:08:22,847
Master,

139
00:08:22,897 --> 00:08:28,280
Could it be that by mistake it got mixed into the
video letters sent to the young ladies last week...?

140
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:31,840
Oh no! I was the one who sent those myself!

141
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:35,560
Aaaah! At this rate,
my world-class presentation!

142
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:38,248
Looks like it's a really important tape

143
00:08:38,298 --> 00:08:40,440
You're so flustered you've
forgotten your ojaru.

144
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:44,560
Why don't you contact them right away and have them send it back,
or go pick it up?

145
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:47,480
The thing is, I don't know who I sent it to.

146
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:51,820
Was it Haruko, or Natsuko,
or Akiko, or maybe Fuyuko?

147
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:57,320
Oh no, the academic presentation is the day after tomorrow.
We only have 48 hours!

148
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:04,120
You only have 48 hours! Where on
earth do your daughters live, anyway?

149
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:07,700
Haruko is cracking down on
poachers in the African jungle...

150
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:12,200
Natsuko is conducting a geological survey
with a submersible in the Bermuda Triangle...

151
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:16,560
Akiko is right now crossing
the North Pole alone by dog sled.

152
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:19,040
Fuyuko is... where was it again?

153
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:23,160
Every last one of them is somewhere crazy!

154
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:26,320
Nyaa... this is terrible!

155
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:29,620
Without that tape, I'm finished.

156
00:09:29,980 --> 00:09:31,320
Let's go and get it.

157
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:33,520
I'll be careful about that too.

158
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:36,880
For the master,
I'd go through fire and water.

159
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:39,200
Let's arrange a plane,
the giant beast Bonga!

160
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:41,700
Hey, Nakagawa, thank you.

161
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:45,720
A trip around the world Sounds fun.

162
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:47,880
Alright, I'm coming too!

163
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:49,920
You two be careful.

164
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:51,580
Hey, hey, did you hear that?

165
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:53,880
Hey, did you hear?

166
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:56,780
Is the tape really that amazing?

167
00:09:56,780 --> 00:09:59,340
He's saying it himself,
so there's no mistake.

168
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:02,300
If we steal that tape,
we can sell it for a fortune.

169
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:05,640
Then we'll be millionaires, boss!

170
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:07,640
Let's go.

171
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:16,200
Sneaky.

172
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,220
Please bear with it.

173
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,880
This is the fastest way.

174
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:32,080
Has your great-grandfather
gone crazy over Africa too?

175
00:10:34,020 --> 00:10:35,940
Africa is wonderful.

176
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:38,340
Look at these animals.

177
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,740
It's a kingdom of the wild!

178
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:43,820
Instead of wrestling with things like that,

179
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:47,060
why don't you act naturally, just like me?

180
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:50,560
Then you'll be able to
talk with the lions too!

181
00:10:50,980 --> 00:10:51,600
Liar!

182
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:53,860
It's not a lie, just watch!

183
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,660
That's a cat!

184
00:11:04,460 --> 00:11:07,000
See? It understood my words!

185
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:08,425
There, there,

186
00:11:08,475 --> 00:11:11,580
I can even do this, you know!

187
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:16,795
How about that?

188
00:11:16,845 --> 00:11:20,060
It's a moving moment where hearts connect!

189
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:23,315
Isn't this all thanks to the old lady

190
00:11:23,365 --> 00:11:25,980
I can do this kind of thing too, you know.

191
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:35,420
At last!

192
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:37,140
We finally caught up.

193
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:38,800
Right, let's go.

194
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:48,020
Master, the coffee is ready.

195
00:11:56,280 --> 00:11:59,460
Arabica, just as I thought.
Th-th-Kilimanjaro, right?

196
00:12:00,060 --> 00:12:02,870
This is no time to be drinking coffee!
Do something about it!

197
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:05,520
Weren't you supposed to
be able to talk to lions?

198
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:08,120
Ah-ah, no need to panic.

199
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,220
Be quiet. It's tea time.

200
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:16,800
Amazing.
The lion is backing off with just one glare.

201
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,100
Master, that was truly magnificent.

202
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:22,700
Didn't I tell you? There's no need to panic.

203
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:25,280
Hey, you were just drinking coffee,
weren't you?

204
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:33,360
Poachers!

205
00:12:34,300 --> 00:12:37,340
You lot! Catch every last one!

206
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:44,160
Hey! Same koi as before!

207
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:50,680
Ugh, you old establishment,
I won't forgive you!

208
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:51,840
Scary!

209
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:55,700
Yes sir! Charge!

210
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:59,400
All of you, follow me!

211
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:10,940
W-what?

212
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:38,080
Yes!

213
00:13:39,190 --> 00:13:40,100
It's this one!

214
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:40,500
San-chan!

215
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:46,240
Uh-oh!

216
00:13:46,340 --> 00:13:46,960
Run!

217
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:50,940
Don't let them get away!

218
00:13:59,220 --> 00:14:00,380
Ugh.

219
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:01,520
Ugh.

220
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:02,900
Ugh.

221
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:04,920
Ugh.

222
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:05,380
Ugh.

223
00:14:05,380 --> 00:14:05,680
Ugh.

224
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:05,960
Ugh.

225
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:06,560
Ugh.

226
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:06,660
Ugh.

227
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:06,780
Ugh.

228
00:14:06,780 --> 00:14:07,780
Ugh.

229
00:14:07,780 --> 00:14:07,900
Ugh.

230
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:08,060
Ugh.

231
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:13,640
Ugh.

232
00:14:14,820 --> 00:14:18,480
Poachers, give up! You're all under arrest!

233
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:20,620
Blessed Buddha!

234
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:22,860
Well, that one...

235
00:14:27,540 --> 00:14:31,060
Weak coffee is American,
strong coffee is African.

236
00:14:45,140 --> 00:14:47,100
Dad's video letter?

237
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:50,280
That was just Dad showing up, though.

238
00:14:51,060 --> 00:14:53,120
Wasn't it at your place?

239
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:54,420
And then...

240
00:14:54,420 --> 00:14:54,780
So that's...

241
00:14:56,760 --> 00:14:58,320
What is the meaning of this!

242
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:15,760
Dad!

243
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:22,480
Are you asking if something
different was on the video letter?

244
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:25,060
This is different,

245
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:32,460
it's a signal.

246
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:46,360
The sea is the mother of all life. I wish I could
show this fantastic undersea symphony to others.

247
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:51,000
Only someone as athletically gifted as you,
sir, could do this.

248
00:15:53,020 --> 00:15:55,760
You were just playing dead, weren't you?

249
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:01,240
Help me!

250
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:05,580
It's right here!

251
00:16:06,260 --> 00:16:08,320
We only have twelve hours left.

252
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:18,320
What's that?

253
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:21,720
Honestly!

254
00:16:22,460 --> 00:16:23,700
Stop!

255
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:39,980
What?

256
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:45,360
A video letter, you say?

257
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:48,340
I accidentally mailed it.

258
00:16:48,390 --> 00:16:50,420
It's an important tape for the conference.

259
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:54,500
I haven't had time to read the letters that came,
but I've brought them all.

260
00:16:57,020 --> 00:16:57,600
That's it!

261
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:00,360
Oh no!

262
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:02,760
Damn it!

263
00:17:03,760 --> 00:17:04,800
Victory for you!

264
00:17:06,580 --> 00:17:08,120
W-why me!

265
00:17:15,820 --> 00:17:17,040
S-senpai!

266
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:22,860
This guy...

267
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:30,240
What? Shut up.

268
00:17:32,580 --> 00:17:34,420
Big bro, something's up with you too

269
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:48,940
How is it, master?

270
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:50,280
This one's wrong too.

271
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:54,640
Then it must be at Fuyuko's place,
but where is Fuyuko right now?

272
00:17:54,640 --> 00:17:56,720
Papa, if it's Fuyuko...

273
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:03,540
Is she really going to space?

274
00:18:11,540 --> 00:18:13,340
Here it is, Papa!

275
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:16,340
I thought something was off.

276
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:20,740
This is it, no doubt about it.

277
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:24,660
Congratulations on finally
achieving your long-held goal, master.

278
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:28,560
But if we don't hurry, there are only
three hours until the presentation!

279
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:43,040
This way, young master.

280
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:43,600
Good work.

281
00:18:45,940 --> 00:18:48,840
From here,
we should reach the venue in thirty minutes.

282
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:50,940
Forty minutes until the presentation.

283
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:52,640
Just in time, then.

284
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:55,660
Hey, you've got the tape with you, right?

285
00:18:55,660 --> 00:18:57,960
If you tell me you lost it
after coming all this way...

286
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:58,820
It's no joke.

287
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:01,820
No need to worry.

288
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:03,460
It's right here.

289
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:10,320
What was that just now?

290
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:13,340
The videotape's been taken!

291
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:14,620
What?

292
00:19:15,940 --> 00:19:18,000
We've got this tape now!

293
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:21,860
The big announcement in my field!

294
00:19:22,040 --> 00:19:24,280
Chase that thief!

295
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:24,960
Alright!

296
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:37,040
Get back here!

297
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:41,360
Yeah, no matter when you visit,
the big city of New York is amazing.

298
00:19:41,360 --> 00:19:43,200
Saying that, Baiga!

299
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:46,400
Master, it's tea time.

300
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:49,845
Hey,

301
00:19:49,895 --> 00:19:54,640
Isn't that beer?

302
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:57,000
In America,
this is what they drink instead of tea.

303
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:09,320
So if you're a lightweight,
don't drink it, got it?

304
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,160
Yeah, it's a traffic jam.

305
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:18,282
Damn it, with that...

306
00:20:18,332 --> 00:20:20,800
We'll use that.

307
00:20:21,640 --> 00:20:23,760
Isn't that Officer Kiba's horse?

308
00:20:23,760 --> 00:20:27,660
Right, Nakagawa,
somehow get Kyojin out to sea.

309
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:29,420
Ah, senpai!

310
00:20:29,420 --> 00:20:32,000
Damn it,

311
00:20:32,050 --> 00:20:34,680
Giddy-up!

312
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:38,660
Dora! Horse thief!

313
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:42,300
Get back here!

314
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:45,700
Give back the tape!

315
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:49,720
Boss! They're chasing us on horseback!

316
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:51,980
Damn, these guys won't quit!

317
00:20:57,380 --> 00:20:59,360
Boss! Roadblock!

318
00:20:59,900 --> 00:21:01,840
Damn! Forced breakthrough!

319
00:21:02,020 --> 00:21:02,820
Stop!

320
00:21:08,660 --> 00:21:09,420
Aaaaaaah!

321
00:21:09,420 --> 00:21:15,980
Aaaaaaah!

322
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:16,040
Aaaaaaah!

323
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:29,120
What is this, a circus or something?

324
00:21:29,580 --> 00:21:32,620
Hey, you lot!

325
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:33,420
Run!

326
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:35,860
Hey, give back the koi!

327
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:38,600
Wait!

328
00:21:45,900 --> 00:21:47,440
What do you think you're doing, you lot!

329
00:21:47,500 --> 00:21:49,220
Shut up! Hand over that swing!

330
00:21:49,540 --> 00:21:51,040
Think you can keep up with us this far?

331
00:21:51,360 --> 00:21:52,280
Here we go, big brother!

332
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:55,040
Damn it!

333
00:22:03,340 --> 00:22:04,440
It's heavy!

334
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:06,540
Whatever you do, don't let go!

335
00:22:07,980 --> 00:22:09,840
Big brother, we're done for!

336
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:20,280
Hey, what are you stealing!

337
00:22:22,220 --> 00:22:23,660
W-what is this!

338
00:22:24,140 --> 00:22:25,600
Granny, what are you doing!

339
00:22:26,060 --> 00:22:27,740
Get the tape back!

340
00:22:28,420 --> 00:22:31,780
Aaaaah! Why me!

341
00:22:37,580 --> 00:22:38,900
Well done!

342
00:22:41,740 --> 00:22:45,420
Master, we've retrieved the tape!

343
00:22:47,940 --> 00:22:49,720
What a granny!

344
00:22:58,180 --> 00:23:01,000
And now, the presentation
by Professor Ezaki Korosuke.

345
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:03,220
First, please take a look at the videotape.

346
00:23:05,260 --> 00:23:06,780
Good thing we made it in time.

347
00:23:06,780 --> 00:23:13,080
After going through hell to get this tape back,
let's see what it's all about.

348
00:23:14,620 --> 00:23:14,980
Me

349
00:23:25,160 --> 00:23:31,060
What's this stupid cartoon? It has
nothing to do with the problem at all!

350
00:23:31,060 --> 00:23:31,620
Me

351
00:23:31,620 --> 00:23:32,220
Impeccable!

352
00:23:36,420 --> 00:23:38,440
Interesting joke!

353
00:23:38,560 --> 00:23:39,280
Bravo!

354
00:23:39,940 --> 00:23:42,180
Interesting joke!

355
00:23:42,680 --> 00:23:44,660
Splendid work, sir!

356
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:47,280
This animation that makes
the whole world laugh!

357
00:23:47,620 --> 00:23:50,220
What was all our hard work for, anyway?

358
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:53,040
Ezaki Korosuke is number one in Japan!

359
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:57,360
Thank you! Thank you! Thank you!

360
00:23:57,360 --> 00:24:01,320
Yeah!

361
00:24:27,360 --> 00:24:29,460
Decided, and inspiration strikes,

362
00:24:29,460 --> 00:24:32,400
bouncing along, gathering it all up,

363
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:35,380
taking action, soaring away,

364
00:24:36,220 --> 00:24:40,200
the most incredible power of all,

365
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:42,620
everyone gather together,

366
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:46,020
if you come here,

367
00:24:46,920 --> 00:24:49,120
like a dream,

368
00:24:49,120 --> 00:24:52,320
the final energy,

369
00:24:53,160 --> 00:24:55,360
gazing at tomorrow,

370
00:24:57,360 --> 00:25:03,420
painting the universe and standing on the ground,
the star of Kameari comes.

371
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:07,140
That should be good enough, right!

372
00:25:07,280 --> 00:25:08,700
No way that's good enough!

373
00:25:20,820 --> 00:25:22,140
It's Maria.

374
00:25:22,660 --> 00:25:25,800
I've been with Ryo-sama for over a year now,

375
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:28,020
and there's been absolutely no progress.

376
00:25:28,020 --> 00:25:30,600
So I asked Komachi and
the others for advice,

377
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:33,780
and they said I just have
to create a fait accompli.

378
00:25:33,780 --> 00:25:36,640
Next time: Maria, Love-Struck Fist!

379
00:25:36,640 --> 00:25:38,020
Look forward to it, darling!

